# dependencies
node_modules/
# intermediate build artifacts (regenerated by npm run ingest)
data/_nodes_*.json
assets/img/images_*.json
assets/icons/_contact_sheet.png
# Ultimatums & Boons DESIGN SOURCES (~1 GB: .afdesign projects + full-res frames).
# The site ships the optimized WebP in assets/ub/ instead — these are kept locally
# for reference only and must never reach the repo (GitHub rejects >100 MB files).
assets/templates/
# The SOURCE RULEBOOKS (~277 MB: nine Grimoire and FAQ PDFs). Same treatment and the same
# reason as the design sources above: they are FFG's copyrighted books, the site's own footer
# says this project is not affiliated with FFG, and republishing them here is the weakest point
# of that. They are yours to keep locally — the pipeline reads them from these folders — and the
# site does not need them: what it serves is the built data/*.json, which ARE committed.
# The folders themselves stay in the repo, each with a README saying which file belongs there.
langs/*/source/*.pdf
langs/*/source_faq/*.pdf
langs/*/source_encounter_ch1/*.pdf
# scratch renders from tools/inspect_pdf.py --grid
assets/img/_inspect-*.png
# test output
a11y-report.json
# Deployment notes — Fernando's own runbook for the VPS, not part of the site.
# Kept locally and used; it just does not belong in the public repo.
deploy.md
# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# OS / editor cruft
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
tools/other